  "story": {
    "headline": "For the First Time, an mRNA Flu Shot Will Be Available to Some People in the United States. Here's What You Should Know",
    "summary": "The Food and Drug Administration just approved the new type of flu vaccine for adults ages 50 and older. It relies on the same technology as many Covid-19 jabs. However, it’s unclear whether insurance companies will pay for the novel flu shot",
    "publisher": "Rally News",
    "url": "https://rally.news/categories/world/?article=For%2Bthe%2BFirst%2BTime%2C%2Ban%2BmRNA%2BFlu%2BShot%2BWill%2BBe%2BAvailable%2Bto%2BSome%2BPeople%2Bin%2Bthe%2BUnited%2BStates.%2BHere%27s%2BWhat%2BYou%2BShould%2BKnow"
  },
  "researchBrief": "The story is corroborated by multiple sources, including AP News, Ars Technica, and TIME. The key claim — that mFlusiva is 27% more effective than traditional flu shots — is supported by a study of 40,000 people, as reported by AP News [apnews.com](https://apnews.com/article/flu-vaccine-moderna-mrna-fda-mflusiva-59d991a6bf70c26e2f0c210cc8ca87f1) and TIME [time.com](https://time.com/article/2026/08/06/fda-approves-first-mrna-flu-vaccine/). The FDA approval for adults 50+ is confirmed by all sources. The uncertainty around insurance coverage is noted in Ars Technica [arstechnica.com](https://arstechnica.com/health/2026/08/modernas-mrna-flu-shot-earns-fda-approval-after-rollercoaster-review/) and TIME [time.com](https://time.com/article/2026/08/06/fda-approves-first-mrna-flu-vaccine/). The faster production time for mRNA vaccines (weeks vs. months for traditional vaccines) is also corroborated by TIME [time.com](https://time.com/article/2026/08/06/fda-approves-first-mrna-flu-vaccine/).",
  "sources": [
    "https://apnews.com/article/flu-vaccine-moderna-mrna-fda-mflusiva-59d991a6bf70c26e2f0c210cc8ca87f1",
    "https://arstechnica.com/health/2026/08/modernas-mrna-flu-shot-earns-fda-approval-after-rollercoaster-review/",
