  "raw": {
    "pillar": "Science & Health Breakthroughs",
    "headline": "Is this the future of flu shots? The FDA just approved a game-changing vaccine — but can you get it?",
    "challenge": "Flu season is coming, and older adults are at higher risk. But traditional flu vaccines take months to produce and aren't always a perfect match for circulating strains. What if there was a faster, more effective option?",
    "solution": "Enter mFlusiva, the first mRNA flu vaccine approved by the FDA! In a major study, it reduced flu cases by 27% compared to other vaccines — and it can be made in weeks, not months. But there's a catch...",
    "resultHeading": "mFlusiva is more effective than traditional flu shots",
    "resultLine": "The FDA approved it, but will insurance cover it? Full details at the link in bio.",
    "whyMatters": "This breakthrough could revolutionize how we fight the flu. mRNA technology means faster production, better strain matching, and potentially stronger protection — especially for those most at risk.",
    "engagementQuestion": "Would you try an mRNA flu shot if it were available to you?",
    "captionLead": "Big news in flu prevention! The FDA just approved the first mRNA flu vaccine, mFlusiva, for adults 50+. It's more effective than traditional shots — but will insurance cover it? Swipe to learn more!",
